  {
    "id": "launchdarkly-comm-1",
    "tier": "community",
    "url": "https://hn.algolia.com/api/v1/items/37611136",
    "excerpt": "LaunchDarkly has a mobile client SDK, but they charge by MAU, which would be untenable. So folks tend to write a proxy for the mobile apps to call.",
    "fetchedAt": "2026-09-05T04:47:08.845Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "launchdarkly-comm-2",
    "tier": "community",
    "url": "https://hn.algolia.com/api/v1/items/37611136",
    "excerpt": "LaunchDarkly clients download all flags in the project on connection, then stream changes. ... LaunchDarkly has an open source 'Relay' you can run in your own environment for extra resiliency.",
    "fetchedAt": "2026-09-05T04:47:08.845Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "launchdarkly-comm-3",
    "tier": "community",
    "url": "https://hn.algolia.com/api/v1/items/37611136",
    "excerpt": "One of the most common things you want to do for a feature flag is ask 'Where is this used in code?' LaunchDarkly even has a product feature that does this, called 'Code References.'",
    "fetchedAt": "2026-09-05T04:47:08.845Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "launchdarkly-comm-4",
    "tier": "community",
    "url": "https://hn.algolia.com/api/v1/items/37611136",
    "excerpt": "If you want an amusing read, go check out LaunchDarkly's 'comparison with Split' page and Split's 'comparison with LaunchDarkly' page. It's especially funny when they make the exact same evaluations, but in reverse.",
    "fetchedAt": "2026-09-05T04:47:08.845Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "launchdarkly-comm-5",
    "tier": "community",
    "url": "https://hn.algolia.com/api/v1/items/12464229",
    "excerpt": "My logs show frequent timeouts when looking up setting through their API. Their SDK default timeout is 3s. Wouldn't want to wait longer.",
    "fetchedAt": "2026-09-05T04:47:08.845Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "launchdarkly-comm-6",
    "tier": "community",
    "url": "https://hn.algolia.com/api/v1/items/12464229",
    "excerpt": "It's a pretty question[able] architecture that outsources feature flags to a third party. You're creating a critical path hard dependency and for most apps this is going to be hit multiple times on every request.",
    "fetchedAt": "2026-09-05T04:47:08.845Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "launchdarkly-comm-7",
    "tier": "community",
    "url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=34692177",
    "excerpt": "Agreed that LaunchDarkly is incredibly over priced.",
    "fetchedAt": "2026-09-05T04:47:08.845Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "launchdarkly-comm-8",
    "tier": "community",
    "url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=13231120",
    "excerpt": "We've used LaunchDarkly (LD) for about a year now. We previously used our own Feature Flag library built by our CTO. LD provided a lot more, and continues to release new features that would've been much more expensive for us to build vs. buy here.",
    "fetchedAt": "2026-09-05T04:47:08.845Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "launchdarkly-comm-9",
    "tier": "community",
    "url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=13231120",
    "excerpt": "Key benefits of LaunchDarkly: rules-based targeting so flags can be set at group level, custom rollout by % of users or attributes, centralized feature flag service via SSE with minimal latency, multivariate flags, and Slack integration for visibility into changes.",
    "fetchedAt": "2026-09-05T04:47:08.845Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "launchdarkly-comm-10",
    "tier": "community",
    "url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=38261351",
    "excerpt": "I have used LaunchDarkly in the past and yeah it's kind of a pain to use.",
    "fetchedAt": "2026-09-05T04:47:08.845Z"
  },
